5. CCDC112 is a gene that is involved male fertility due to its role in mitochondiral morphogenesis and sheath formation. 
  If we knock down this gene, it will result in male sterility due to the abnormal mitochondrial sheath of sperm and reduced ATP,
  which would affect the function and motility of sperm. Essentially, the sperm would not have enough energy to move and reach fertilization.
  The phenotype would be the reduced sperm motility.
  Source for CCDC112: https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.1101/2024.11.05.622046v1.full
